[{:db/id "q-122608/selection/74f74a71fc8530eb557ab2f14cc876df8a1cf0f0bf56a13330009a232cc25452" :answer/id #uuid "f2724265-4796-5dcc-87a9-83ced534fcf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122608/selection/12882a91fc2ee476c02a2d34ba6502cb3a9a45f24c91cc29657d351bd72aa71d" :answer/id #uuid "17a82dea-a4d0-5418-8d80-ddd7fc43decd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122608/selection/37cf0bdb15f0ba4cdb22ae63b47f612099e1616a06888e8953f1b9eb5b32ecc2" :answer/id #uuid "65b17c73-f96d-58b3-ba74-036e204f51ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2y{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122608/selection/77b24a5b1a978f6a090868844aa7bb2fbd05d0fcf5fc65f5be596b8829f89a96" :answer/id #uuid "441bdf44-67a6-5746-b35e-310b1a1074ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122608/selection/955688ef6b776f36e3dc4d6db222b435c3ee41040c62a852be89040ed7a0314e" :answer/id #uuid "f4fbd5ae-a952-50f4-a41d-a4db7564ce14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122608/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fc36121-4553-5759-80a8-37f10821ef73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122608/selection/955688ef6b776f36e3dc4d6db222b435c3ee41040c62a852be89040ed7a0314e" :answer-field/choices ["q-122608/selection/74f74a71fc8530eb557ab2f14cc876df8a1cf0f0bf56a13330009a232cc25452" "q-122608/selection/12882a91fc2ee476c02a2d34ba6502cb3a9a45f24c91cc29657d351bd72aa71d" "q-122608/selection/37cf0bdb15f0ba4cdb22ae63b47f612099e1616a06888e8953f1b9eb5b32ecc2" "q-122608/selection/77b24a5b1a978f6a090868844aa7bb2fbd05d0fcf5fc65f5be596b8829f89a96" "q-122608/selection/955688ef6b776f36e3dc4d6db222b435c3ee41040c62a852be89040ed7a0314e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122608" :question/id #uuid "b9b6323d-ff08-50ce-be1a-fa1f61c66864" :question/math-academy-id "q-122608" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & =-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd5c5fd8-409c-5b92-a0f1-4466c76cdbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122607/selection/daffd98a47259f36978edc1f91f98198db1ceccb9dc0a09831d55ec0b5d16fdb" :answer/id #uuid "66d65423-8e2f-5da4-81f9-ea65d314b6f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2y+1}}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122607/selection/2675cd3856fa4153ded7aada20640a04927c7cfdfc49f796e6aae5611f7f2b66" :answer/id #uuid "86df8729-4b86-5d65-9616-5b55d5563623" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122607/selection/3d6bc97db4a199940013fa7381129fc4fa20f11507929e678289623126bea779" :answer/id #uuid "7c47da1e-eb32-5bb5-8699-c2f93a2cb998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122607/selection/339cef4c9c4f221493a8b3dd5b03cea0cda550b36ebfedc0f061132ece8db6fa" :answer/id #uuid "3e07973b-7cab-5bc0-93dc-1c33a30bd745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2y+1}}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122607/selection/709a9420e40e2037cd999cdd3c44f7c2ce64b68108db7bb51ba57edd44e5fa8e" :answer/id #uuid "93125115-7ba2-54bf-a769-1d3723b5435c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90150a42-a85f-5de2-9664-4071fac74367" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122607/selection/2675cd3856fa4153ded7aada20640a04927c7cfdfc49f796e6aae5611f7f2b66" :answer-field/choices ["q-122607/selection/daffd98a47259f36978edc1f91f98198db1ceccb9dc0a09831d55ec0b5d16fdb" "q-122607/selection/2675cd3856fa4153ded7aada20640a04927c7cfdfc49f796e6aae5611f7f2b66" "q-122607/selection/3d6bc97db4a199940013fa7381129fc4fa20f11507929e678289623126bea779" "q-122607/selection/339cef4c9c4f221493a8b3dd5b03cea0cda550b36ebfedc0f061132ece8db6fa" "q-122607/selection/709a9420e40e2037cd999cdd3c44f7c2ce64b68108db7bb51ba57edd44e5fa8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122607" :question/id #uuid "fc89b308-add9-53d2-a586-2eb622cde5b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122607" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd5c5fd8-409c-5b92-a0f1-4466c76cdbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122600/selection/3a1f121902223cba076a05e7443c0193cce7e674b06125b99efbe44e62dcb665" :answer/id #uuid "cce43dcb-ff6c-5dea-9b2a-827f856310a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(z+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+(x+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122600/selection/9e2aafadd2d3c2f99d104f93e1ac506986f3613ec9c29f071f099c60beaefaf2" :answer/id #uuid "93b30ebb-5a2c-5602-8673-de03e4241a29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122600/selection/ad6c186507397d4035f9c6002a201c5e285b6f9ba25a658c53709e648495f9f1" :answer/id #uuid "8752c14d-a01d-59fe-86c0-7feda71cd455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122600/selection/adc7d280ac4f39b5dafa4b06f943e4f542dccba07605e400610cadd0a41b1acb" :answer/id #uuid "df6eec77-6efd-5a21-96ac-938400b79711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122600/selection/b304bb0126235fef7e83658a0c92b6fd497f82714ebbffddabdcfd2ef2de9f91" :answer/id #uuid "8230c9e9-bdc5-5860-86a7-be1d7aa0dbee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122600/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa79643-983b-5cc6-9b1d-13948241112b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122600/selection/9e2aafadd2d3c2f99d104f93e1ac506986f3613ec9c29f071f099c60beaefaf2" :answer-field/choices ["q-122600/selection/3a1f121902223cba076a05e7443c0193cce7e674b06125b99efbe44e62dcb665" "q-122600/selection/9e2aafadd2d3c2f99d104f93e1ac506986f3613ec9c29f071f099c60beaefaf2" "q-122600/selection/ad6c186507397d4035f9c6002a201c5e285b6f9ba25a658c53709e648495f9f1" "q-122600/selection/adc7d280ac4f39b5dafa4b06f943e4f542dccba07605e400610cadd0a41b1acb" "q-122600/selection/b304bb0126235fef7e83658a0c92b6fd497f82714ebbffddabdcfd2ef2de9f91"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122600" :question/id #uuid "cde4da3d-ec55-5f32-ac16-c33bd9acfbfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122600" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y) \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122600/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd5c5fd8-409c-5b92-a0f1-4466c76cdbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122600"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122404"] :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{z-2y} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i-\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122596/selection/8fac0010707688e81b8418c6588fb0dfad9ac1cc52d099ba8db8ceb4ad51f0b9" :answer/id #uuid "54025300-03d6-58a3-b3c9-56f1cd5ca096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "yz\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+xz\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+xy\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122596/selection/c6c8c7e46cf6961f5d1a4b3653e3d3420ccfaf3dbc592c9b14988c82f722d815" :answer/id #uuid "139bdfa4-1f8c-59c7-8384-b23584b0efb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+2y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+2z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122596/selection/4374728a45b0598ffdc278c4e3ec8b3cfa5178d7610d5cc08bf2eeaf4565d8e6" :answer/id #uuid "eb00b5d5-b00f-59cb-acb2-28c38512ab8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122596/selection/ac873823f14bc36313425ac11ae0cc4c25300e0d7d1b8ae7170072d933d039d2" :answer/id #uuid "1379c18b-ba1c-5d46-b926-1da867f05c97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{yz}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{xz}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122596/selection/f41e8b7a956294b384febbf16324c99e20d223b28f45f701a6d6e45ca87b41b9" :answer/id #uuid "3dd13b1a-105a-574d-b550-d9d4dfd0bbdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2xz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122596/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8bc395-67b6-55b7-880b-49b60e71b422" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122596/selection/4374728a45b0598ffdc278c4e3ec8b3cfa5178d7610d5cc08bf2eeaf4565d8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-122596/selection/8fac0010707688e81b8418c6588fb0dfad9ac1cc52d099ba8db8ceb4ad51f0b9" "q-122596/selection/c6c8c7e46cf6961f5d1a4b3653e3d3420ccfaf3dbc592c9b14988c82f722d815" "q-122596/selection/4374728a45b0598ffdc278c4e3ec8b3cfa5178d7610d5cc08bf2eeaf4565d8e6" "q-122596/selection/ac873823f14bc36313425ac11ae0cc4c25300e0d7d1b8ae7170072d933d039d2" "q-122596/selection/f41e8b7a956294b384febbf16324c99e20d223b28f45f701a6d6e45ca87b41b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122596" :question/id #uuid "a300dd68-88af-507e-9066-e4497e289afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-122596" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122596/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd5c5fd8-409c-5b92-a0f1-4466c76cdbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122699/selection/31220df95428bdce78ce558753c5353dc9bc6bf171f585c8a3f3ccc47b7ef735" :answer/id #uuid "3648a022-3fb7-5a0b-a02e-2822033cfc59" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/df6472974d246217341c69163c2336190980b5aacaa5b1a5c11cbb7126ddde86.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122699/selection/ff8e677d5efbb6cb91c00cd502c8ae69d4232a46e68d4a2083396b09c13d6f58" :answer/id #uuid "87777c72-a74c-596f-b251-14e9d73f7a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/0f45b194df67a060c195d4368050cdad9b8bfefab86b41d5eb63723631543d7b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122699/selection/720f7aa0e978564810abea6f44e3f271a81727b2472318d46cb111bdd2ba5834" :answer/id #uuid "6147ad45-5d20-5769-ac9e-6d01c7d98d74" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122699/selection/f78b4a56823db0d2110eef947520aa783b5dadfc87af869fd9b8fcc79f874064" :answer/id #uuid "32448c40-e06a-58e3-be5a-38374fc25c69" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/7618ae208ba53f12fb31988a3e0d0cb40f78ddc4348c5049bb09127039c4d965.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122699/selection/5bd976fe60415b8cda027a275ee1e426ee864cb4b478e762e7bf0e6f310b679b" :answer/id #uuid "d24f51e8-9ff8-51ce-9a27-8dcb023c627c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/6c76d43daa86b2c8034e3f12592ee6c18bc533034cb255934ff7eb08b2d53623.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd745c4b-76db-5536-a918-e965edb45b2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122699/selection/720f7aa0e978564810abea6f44e3f271a81727b2472318d46cb111bdd2ba5834" :answer-field/choices ["q-122699/selection/31220df95428bdce78ce558753c5353dc9bc6bf171f585c8a3f3ccc47b7ef735" "q-122699/selection/ff8e677d5efbb6cb91c00cd502c8ae69d4232a46e68d4a2083396b09c13d6f58" "q-122699/selection/720f7aa0e978564810abea6f44e3f271a81727b2472318d46cb111bdd2ba5834" "q-122699/selection/f78b4a56823db0d2110eef947520aa783b5dadfc87af869fd9b8fcc79f874064" "q-122699/selection/5bd976fe60415b8cda027a275ee1e426ee864cb4b478e762e7bf0e6f310b679b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122699" :question/id #uuid "bef9da0c-f04d-5f81-acd5-4bdc3f69bc23" :question/math-academy-id "q-122699" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2y-x?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-x) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-x) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,2),$ $(2,2),$ and $(2,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-2) & =-i+2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a43f82e-6682-56af-994a-b0bdf12b4095"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122619/selection/cb2da2857a457b0a137f50cb628e45f4d94c4a747bc9ae8a6d2a3adc2c31bb11" :answer/id #uuid "d37343ed-1795-5b3e-b35a-c57b2a1a2b01" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/0d5f1fb1b13459937f7bd3ff0ed8b6da641fcd346dc961d7ec5b98be29e45b1d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122619/selection/916d9487e1deca917dcef8464c29dffc4f68b5da7f908c8d1066f0a3e9742de5" :answer/id #uuid "3621f069-2b56-567e-be82-fe8d3abfd4b2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/8a35641fa57b01a95a0c1d5b3dba8a0072b291a6822ac7b2f5e0473b9037796b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122619/selection/ff15b086b4d550a623230747409b8fd12602a17a76dc891c2e39467905288cdb" :answer/id #uuid "bc0d1654-e23b-5e72-a437-76d5fc83daae" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122619/selection/7fac05d735e70e26f5110a823e69b9eb34f091d472e80f87d2f0eacabb6445ed" :answer/id #uuid "fc51555c-7d4f-5501-86c8-f0532f79b1bb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/cdebaf3d8c07fe6cb26c4fb2c5b72d2bd60dc968b3345fc1c4a5737d8c6c2b53.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122619/selection/9fa11bdf3bc0ee657a9636c75cd71ab3988706ed25d163dfab20f1394644a524" :answer/id #uuid "5bdb5fd7-31de-52cb-86df-63085ef18703" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/acb2066428e0660e7d4e106acd5faf60600d6f93de0b6cf4c43ee2b5864e6e51.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122619/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "291055da-c7ad-530c-bc99-a830a0c768ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122619/selection/ff15b086b4d550a623230747409b8fd12602a17a76dc891c2e39467905288cdb" :answer-field/choices ["q-122619/selection/cb2da2857a457b0a137f50cb628e45f4d94c4a747bc9ae8a6d2a3adc2c31bb11" "q-122619/selection/916d9487e1deca917dcef8464c29dffc4f68b5da7f908c8d1066f0a3e9742de5" "q-122619/selection/ff15b086b4d550a623230747409b8fd12602a17a76dc891c2e39467905288cdb" "q-122619/selection/7fac05d735e70e26f5110a823e69b9eb34f091d472e80f87d2f0eacabb6445ed" "q-122619/selection/9fa11bdf3bc0ee657a9636c75cd71ab3988706ed25d163dfab20f1394644a524"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122619" :question/id #uuid "40689dc7-e924-59ea-9bdd-9f2acdedd9ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-122619" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\,i+2y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-4,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(3,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-4,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,-1) & =i+2\\cdot (-1)\\,j=i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122619/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a43f82e-6682-56af-994a-b0bdf12b4095"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122619"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122713/selection/a894fe49247349effeef00861fe055af0b72e0f01628252048e1265458fbfc57" :answer/id #uuid "cdbcc262-d67b-597e-b50e-840d9565cbe9" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Develope