dio :answer-field/correct "q-122713/selection/91fc15ad19bba2bd5b38c88fe67e4b5ba4facef4146dd078c55b9999076b5707" :answer-field/choices ["q-122713/selection/a894fe49247349effeef00861fe055af0b72e0f01628252048e1265458fbfc57" "q-122713/selection/91fc15ad19bba2bd5b38c88fe67e4b5ba4facef4146dd078c55b9999076b5707" "q-122713/selection/c8ea4ba9281b924a4e3affed2245f2974b77b1e06cb4bfd4d7591b43ce49f2f0" "q-122713/selection/1fb4537eeb69db30d65b68927b0184be793c82a4d6ec53085a47d2fe5e77db78" "q-122713/selection/391e244e46bb70bb7bb4d1d89a0e29c2087f446fa10913912fb86025d8b9fb1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122713" :question/id #uuid "91cb20d9-0768-57d2-91f5-f873cc45139d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122713" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),$ $(0,-2),$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,1) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,j=i-j \\\\ ∇f(0,-2) & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-2)}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,j=-4\\,i \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,j=4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122713/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a43f82e-6682-56af-994a-b0bdf12b4095"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122713"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122789"] :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,2),$ $(2,-3),$ and $(2,1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,2) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-2)^{2}\\,i-2\\,j=3\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-3) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}\\,i-(-3)\\,j=3\\,i+3\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}\\,i-\\,j=3\\,i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/26a5c0123d93231a800456e9f06f6ba7450861838c87d4d1b3ae77dab4cec6cf.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122738/selection/23e4a71c5af9b6655035f7ae7f9b51784e7b98a88ddf253bd8cdb7b0ae3abc01" :answer/id #uuid "8cfb882f-61ae-5fcb-b39f-f56482f72c48" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/135122e85da455699e45c1e276152b20fee0ac9d18441eb5620b1aa43654c81b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122738/selection/f8c173d7f95836c3786ba79e789644e713147d4ab5df3ddba4557c3cb6921b54" :answer/id #uuid "eccd7b27-c4cf-5f5c-80ae-4bd6aa53c0b6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/e4f9011d4497ac01495c1dcde81d9ba19e9b48f9d78c36ca6259d3a2465983b7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122738/selection/ad68a6a6f1bc5f2edb549f865e0978d60e88cd8e61bbf3e85505c220caa03b98" :answer/id #uuid "17492e81-8fc6-50ef-92c8-e5c39b447cb3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/716f99a985d8b4909e76f922fc3bf5b3350f9cb7496ae0a0a429421016a19267.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122738/selection/b30aab673f3bb0cbd272c7dff2d740f53d946b16d388a9702b96dbe8281826dc" :answer/id #uuid "a91dc664-0612-5d1a-91eb-17624ed415b1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/2595c11a1b30fee9d76028010d2c7e608250c0d48ce0191d7da2a5412af6a110.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122738/selection/6e4c53ea1a521b2c348144707585c6267914ca43665db412caf6e570359f89a4" :answer/id #uuid "ff5b8f09-fc3a-5da3-b2ac-c024251d6116" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/3bf6311586ae40bb490414108bbf232f40e1e727da45bbdbe3123e60c17f6268.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122738/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7562ddb-6882-5063-a19d-c44e6874ae0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122738/selection/b30aab673f3bb0cbd272c7dff2d740f53d946b16d388a9702b96dbe8281826dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-122738/selection/23e4a71c5af9b6655035f7ae7f9b51784e7b98a88ddf253bd8cdb7b0ae3abc01" "q-122738/selection/f8c173d7f95836c3786ba79e789644e713147d4ab5df3ddba4557c3cb6921b54" "q-122738/selection/ad68a6a6f1bc5f2edb549f865e0978d60e88cd8e61bbf3e85505c220caa03b98" "q-122738/selection/b30aab673f3bb0cbd272c7dff2d740f53d946b16d388a9702b96dbe8281826dc" "q-122738/selection/6e4c53ea1a521b2c348144707585c6267914ca43665db412caf6e570359f89a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122738" :question/id #uuid "f24a7d35-55d7-535e-816a-4ff2815ba4bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-122738" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2(y-2x) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =y-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-2(y-2x)\\,i+(y-2x)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(1,1),$ $(1,3),$ and $(-2,-3).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,1) & =-2\\cdot (1-2\\cdot 1)\\,i+(1-2\\cdot 1)\\,j=2\\,i-j \\\\ ∇f(1,3) & =-2\\cdot (3-2\\cdot 1)\\,i+(3-2\\cdot 1)\\,j=-2\\,i+j \\\\ ∇f(-2,-3) & =-2\\cdot (-3-2\\cdot (-2))\\,i+(-3-2\\cdot (-2))\\,j=-2\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/2595c11a1b30fee9d76028010d2c7e608250c0d48ce0191d7da2a5412af6a110.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122738/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a43f82e-6682-56af-994a-b0bdf12b4095"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122738"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122790/selection/7432123aeacd2b8ae938cce3db65362a17120e3b9a1e45a1b31fb53ee8d86e93" :answer/id #uuid "1b784233-a0fa-5165-bcd8-17603f10b5c0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/417f9bd99ad7032ffac7ce258c5122d932b1bb1610237ef030f077ca56815bec.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122790/selection/1c0348b4d8b88f7ed7ec37eea83871fe5830dccaf14df347a971aae657b5c2bd" :answer/id #uuid "1b6ea7be-fd16-503a-9e7d-1c8a380bde94" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/ae9e6dc29361d66784dae2868e500940132049cfa04b65aafddc06d35c1afdbf.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122790/selection/10215be455422420d457f48095911d1dbac69f88f9308eb05c27860ba9ec01fc" :answer/id #uuid "b4728745-187d-5637-9ac0-5be8b92ef4fc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/00b722a09fef4428d17fc7ff6a301b3860e798b20c44126b63cd381ad2884398.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122790/selection/3b3d8e526aefe5a951f1eb07aa5f4c4d1a3295a4eadb4c5e0896d84bb5aadc41" :a